Navigation note (covenant #7 — no predecessor bypass): the web route /timeline has no pre-existing AppRoute case or
AppRouteParser alias. A dedicated .timeline case was ADDED to the AppRoute enum (mirroring its sibling analytics
sub-pages .fleetCompare / .lifetimeStats / .mileage / .tco, which each own a route). Its default pathSegment is
"timeline" so AppRouteParser.parse("/timeline") resolves to it with no alias needed; it joins the .insights sidebar
group. TimelineRouteRegistration.registry(.timeline) fills its host. The parser's existing aliases, every sibling
registration, and the registry chain are otherwise untouched. RouteTests (unique-path-segment + every-route-in-its-
group) remain satisfied. The page model is built @MainActor in the registration enum and captured, mirroring the
sibling *RouteRegistration enums.

